--------------------------------
PLAYWRIGHT SPECIAL LOCATORS
--------------------------------

Playwright provides special locators to locate elements using
user-facing information such as:

→ Label
→ Placeholder
→ Role
→ Text

In this topic, we are learning:

1. getByLabel()
2. getByPlaceholder()
3. getByRole()
4. getByText()


--------------------------------
COMPLETE CODE
--------------------------------

import { expect, test } from '@playwright/test';

test('should locate elements using special locators', async ({ page }) => {

    await page.goto('https://rahulshettyacademy.com/angularpractice/');

    await page.getByLabel('Check me out').click();

    await page.getByLabel('Employed').check();

    await page.getByLabel('Gender').selectOption('Female');

    await page.getByPlaceholder('Password').fill('password123');

    await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();

    await expect(
        page.getByText('Success! The Form has been submitted successfully!.')
    ).toBeVisible();

    await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Home' }).click();

    await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Shop' }).click();

    await page.pause();
});


